1
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:10,630
Come in.

2
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,840
I've been waiting for you.

3
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:17,510
Hi, I just...

4
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:20,640
Ah! Oh, my God! Monica!

5
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:22,430
Oh, my God!

6
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,520
I'm sorry! I was...

7
00:00:24,690 --> 00:00:25,980
I was taking a nap.

8
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:29,440
Since when do you take naps in that position?

9
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:34,530
Tell me you were waiting for a guy. Please tell me.

10
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:37,820
Yes, I was. A guy.

11
00:00:37,990 --> 00:00:39,740
From work.

12
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:42,750
I'm seeing a guy from work! Ha!

13
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:46,750
That cute waiter guy from your restaurant.

14
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,040
The one that looks like a non-threatening Ray Liotta?

15
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,000
Aha. That one!

16
00:00:52,170 --> 00:00:55,920
Give me a second. I'll be out of your hair. I'm just going to grab a jacket.

17
00:00:56,090 --> 00:01:00,050
When I get back, I want every little detail.

18
00:01:02,970 --> 00:01:04,350
Maybe that's him.

19
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:07,350
Okay, um... Okay, um...

20
00:01:08,810 --> 00:01:11,230
It's just Joey and Ross.

21
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:12,820
Why aren't you at the movie?

22
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:16,400
We were, but Ross was talking so loud on his phone, they threw us out.

23
00:01:16,570 --> 00:01:20,030
I had to talk loud because the movie was loud!

24
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:25,790
- He's talking to London.      - Did he get in touch with Emily?

25
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:28,080
No. He's calling everyone on her side of the family...

26
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:30,420
...hoping someone will help him get in touch with her.

27
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:36,220
I don't care if I said some other girl's name, you prissy old twit!

28
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:37,800
Ross.

29
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:40,300
Way to suck up to the family!

30
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:52,900
I'm so glad you're all here. My office finally got wrinkle-free fax paper!

31
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:47,620
- Hey      - Oh, no, no! Vomit tux! No, no! Vomit tux!

32
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:49,870
Don't worry, I had it dry-cleaned.

33
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,080
Vomit tux?

34
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:53,460
Who vomited on...

35
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:56,840
You know what? What you up to, Joe?

36
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:59,720
They're doing this telethon thing on TV.

37
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:02,470
And my agent got me a job as co-host!

38
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,180
That's great!

39
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:08,270
A little good deed for PBS, plus some TV exposure.

40
00:03:08,430 --> 00:03:11,730
That's the kind of math Joey likes to do.

41
00:03:12,850 --> 00:03:15,020
Oh, PBS!

42
00:03:15,190 --> 00:03:18,030
- What's wrong with PBS?     - What's right with them?

43
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:21,320
Why don't you like PBS?

44
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:26,910
Right after my Mom killed herself, I was in this bad place, you know, personally.

45
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:31,710
So I just thought it would make me feel better if I wrote to Sesame Street.

46
00:03:31,870 --> 00:03:34,790
Because they were so nice when I was a little kid.

47
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,920
No one ever wrote back.

48
00:03:37,090 --> 00:03:40,260
A lot of those Muppets don't have thumbs.

49
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:46,050
All I got was a lousy keychain, and by that time, I was living in a box.

50
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:48,100
I didn't have keys!

51
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:50,520
I'm sorry, Pheebs.

52
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:54,020
I just wanted to do a good deed, like you did with the babies.

53
00:03:54,190 --> 00:03:58,520
This isn't a good deed. You just want to get on TV. This is totally selfish.

54
00:03:58,730 --> 00:04:00,150
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

55
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:02,820
What about you having those babies for your brother?

56
00:04:02,990 --> 00:04:04,570
Talk about selfish!

57
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:08,280
What are you talking about?

58
00:04:08,450 --> 00:04:11,700
It was a nice thing, but it made you feel good, right?

59
00:04:11,870 --> 00:04:13,120
Yeah, so?

60
00:04:13,290 --> 00:04:16,040
It made you feel good so that makes it selfish.

61
00:04:16,210 --> 00:04:19,750
Look, there's no unselfish good deeds. Sorry.

62
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:23,670
Yes, there are totally good deeds that are selfless!

63
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:25,760
May I ask for one example?

64
00:04:25,930 --> 00:04:28,640
Yeah, it's... You know, there's...

65
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:30,760
No, you may not!

66
00:04:32,350 --> 00:04:34,600
That's because all people are selfish.

67
00:04:34,770 --> 00:04:36,810
Are you calling me selfish?

68
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:39,690
Are you calling you people?

69
00:04:41,070 --> 00:04:45,780
Sorry to burst that bubble, Pheebs, but selfless good deeds don't exist.

70
00:04:45,950 --> 00:04:46,990
Okay?

71
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,990
And you know the deal on Santa Claus, right?

72
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:54,910
I'm gonna find a selfless good deed. I'm going to beat you, you evil genius!

73
00:04:57,710 --> 00:05:00,000
- Hello?     - Hello, Ross?

74
00:05:00,170 --> 00:05:01,380
Emily?

75
00:05:01,550 --> 00:05:03,920
Oh, my God! It's Emily!

76
00:05:04,090 --> 00:05:06,170
It's Emily, everyone! Shh! Shh! Shh!

77
00:05:07,970 --> 00:05:09,470
Hi.

78
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:13,350
I'm only ringing to say stop harassing my relatives. Goodbye.

79
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:18,730
Wait! Okay, okay, you can hang up, but I'll keep calling everyone in England...

80
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:21,400
...if that's what it takes to get you to talk to me.

81
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:23,280
Really? About what?

82
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:25,860
Look, you're my wife. We're married.

83
00:05:26,030 --> 00:05:28,110
You know, I love you.

84
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:30,660
I really miss you.

85
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,490
I miss you too.

86
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:35,870
Well, at least I think I do.

87
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:37,710
She's talking.

88
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:46,420
When you said "the deal with Santa Claus," you meant?

89
00:05:46,590 --> 00:05:48,050
That he doesn't exist.

90
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,800
Right.

91
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:57,730
Chandler, have you heard about Monica's secret boyfriend?

92
00:05:57,890 --> 00:06:01,900
Yeah, she might have mentioned him.

93
00:06:02,650 --> 00:06:06,900
So, Mon, when are we going to meet this new, secret waiter man?

94
00:06:07,070 --> 00:06:10,320
He's really shy. I don't think he's up to meeting everyone yet.

95
00:06:10,490 --> 00:06:12,910
Yeah, I don't think he's up to meeting everyone yet.

96
00:06:13,450 --> 00:06:17,500
I don't care, I wanna meet this guy who's the best sex she ever had.

97
00:06:18,710 --> 00:06:20,420
Really?

98
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:24,420
That's what you heard? You said that?

99
00:06:24,590 --> 00:06:26,090
I might have said that.

100
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:30,760
Why is that funny?

101
00:06:31,590 --> 00:06:34,430
Because I'm very happy for him.

102
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:37,220
And you! You lucky dog!

103
00:06:39,730 --> 00:06:41,140
- Hi.     - Hey.

104
00:06:41,310 --> 00:06:43,730
Well, Emily's willing to work on the relationship.

105
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:45,150
- That's great!     - Yes!

106
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:46,400
In London.

107
00:06:46,570 --> 00:06:49,440
- What?      - She wants me to move to London.

108
00:06:49,610 --> 00:06:50,700
But you live here.

109
00:06:53,990 --> 00:06:55,740
You know that.

110
00:06:57,290 --> 00:06:58,580
What are you gonna do?

111
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,670
I bet if I talked to Carol and Susan...

112
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:05,750
...I could convince them to move to London with Ben.

113
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:08,920
I'm sure your ex-wife would be more than happy to move to another country...

114
00:07:09,090 --> 00:07:11,760
...so you can patch things up with your new wife.

115
00:07:13,970 --> 00:07:15,970
It could happen.

116
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:23,810
How you doing? Welcome. Good to see you.

117
00:07:24,770 --> 00:07:26,400
This'll be your phone.

118
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,700
That's great.

119
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:34,870
But I'm not really expecting a lot of calls.

120
00:07:35,370 --> 00:07:37,530
No, you answer it and take pledges.

121
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:39,040
But I'm the host.

122
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:43,080
No, Gary Collins is the host. You'll be answering the phone.

123
00:07:44,290 --> 00:07:48,420
You don't seem to understand. See, I was Dr. Drake Ramoray.

124
00:07:48,590 --> 00:07:51,130
Well, here's your phone, doctor.

125
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:56,640
I can't believe I can't find a selfless good deed.

126
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:59,310
You know that really old guy that lives next door to me?

127
00:07:59,470 --> 00:08:02,810
I snuck over there and raked up all the leaves on his front stoop.

128
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:07,230
But he caught me, and he force-fed me cider and cookies.

129
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:12,650
Then I felt wonderful. That old jackass!

130
00:08:12,820 --> 00:08:16,530
Maybe Joey's right. Maybe all good deeds are selfish.

131
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:20,160
I will find a selfless good deed. Because I just gave birth to three children...

132
00:08:20,330 --> 00:08:24,250
...and I will not let them be raised in a world where Joey's right!

133
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:28,080
Hey, Monica? Can I ask you a cooking question?

134
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:31,550
- Sure.     - If you're cooking on the stove...

135
00:08:31,710 --> 00:08:35,630
...does that mean that your new secret boyfriend is better in bed than Richard?

136
00:08:36,550 --> 00:08:38,850
Chandler.

137
00:08:39,850 --> 00:08:41,220
Is he?

138
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:47,350
I think I'm going to respect the privacy of my new, secret boyfriend.

139
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:49,770
Why?

140
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,780
If this guy was me...

141
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:57,240
...and it's me who'd learned that it was me who was the best you'd ever had...

142
00:08:57,410 --> 00:08:58,780
...I'd be going like this

143
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:10,090
All right, Emily.

144
00:09:10,250 --> 00:09:12,130
As much as I love you...

145
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:15,840
...I'm sorry, I can't move to London without Ben.

146
00:09:16,010 --> 00:09:18,930
I understand that would be difficult.

147
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:22,890
Would you consider moving here? You were moving here anyway.

148
00:09:23,060 --> 00:09:25,270
Why can't you just do that?

149
00:09:25,430 --> 00:09:27,520
I don't know. It's just...

150
00:09:27,690 --> 00:09:34,530
Okay, okay, but I know that even though I've been a complete idiot up till now...

151
00:09:34,690 --> 00:09:36,530
...you have to come here.

152
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:40,280
You have to, so we can work this out together.

153
00:09:40,870 --> 00:09:42,240
All right.

154
00:09:42,410 --> 00:09:44,950
All right? Did you just say "all right"?

155
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:47,710
I did. Now I'm the idiot.

156
00:09:48,210 --> 00:09:50,040
Emily, that is so great!

157
00:09:50,210 --> 00:09:51,420
It'll be great!

158
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:55,590
We're going to be like two idiots in love!

159
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:02,100
Ross, there's one thing that really scares me still.

160
00:10:02,260 --> 00:10:04,760
- Yes, tell me.     - You have to understand...

161
00:10:04,930 --> 00:10:07,230
...how humiliating it was for me up on that altar...

162
00:10:07,390 --> 00:10:10,270
...in front of my entire family, all my friends.

163
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:13,440
I know. I am so sorry.

164
00:10:13,610 --> 00:10:17,440
And then, after deciding to forgive you...

165
00:10:17,610 --> 00:10:21,030
...seeing you at the airport, catching our plane with her.

166
00:10:21,530 --> 00:10:24,700
Again, very sorry.

167
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:29,000
I mean, I can't be in the same room as her.

168
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:32,880
It drives me mad thinking of you being in the same room as her.

169
00:10:33,630 --> 00:10:37,340
Emily, there is nothing between Rachel and me.

170
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:38,880
Okay?

171
00:10:39,050 --> 00:10:41,010
I love you.

172
00:10:42,050 --> 00:10:43,850
All right.

173
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:47,890
I'll come to New York and we'll try to make this work.

174
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:49,480
That is so great!

175
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:53,310
As long as you don't see Rachel anymore.

176
00:11:00,450 --> 00:11:04,030
I asked Emily if she would come to New York.

177
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,830
And she said yes.

178
00:11:05,990 --> 00:11:08,750
- Great!     - No, no, no.

179
00:11:09,290 --> 00:11:12,620
Only if I promise never to see Rachel again.

180
00:11:12,790 --> 00:11:14,290
What? You can't...

181
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:15,540
What did you tell her?

182
00:11:15,710 --> 00:11:17,590
I told her I'd have to think about it.

183
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:20,970
I mean, how the hell am I supposed to make this kind of a decision?

184
00:11:22,340 --> 00:11:24,640
I'm actually asking you!

185
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:28,010
Well, you can't just not see Rachel anymore.

186
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:30,140
She's one of your best friends.

187
00:11:30,310 --> 00:11:32,980
But he can't not see Emily, I mean that's his wife!

188
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:34,400
- That's true!     - Yeah, right?

189
00:11:35,190 --> 00:11:37,000
But you've known Rachel since high school and...

190
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,440
you cannot just cut her out of your life.

191
00:11:39,610 --> 00:11:41,490
- That's true!      - No, you cannot.

192
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:45,570
Thanks for the help. Problem solved!

193
00:11:50,620 --> 00:11:52,040
- Hello?     - Hey, Mon.

194
00:11:52,210 --> 00:11:55,460
Oh, hey, Joey. We've been watching all day. When are you gonna be on TV?

195
00:11:56,210 --> 00:11:59,210
There was kind of a mix-up in my agent's office...

196
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:01,880
...but I'm still on TV, and that's good exposure.

197
00:12:03,130 --> 00:12:04,380
You're not on TV.

198
00:12:07,050 --> 00:12:09,930
Oh, okay. How about now?

199
00:12:11,930 --> 00:12:14,020
Yeah! There he is! There he is!

200
00:12:14,190 --> 00:12:16,480
Hello, New York!

201
00:12:18,270 --> 00:12:21,400
Maybe just put the whole duck right in there. Who cares?

202
00:12:21,570 --> 00:12:24,400
- Now I got the legs.     - Aw! Aw!

203
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:32,160
How many times have I told you guys to never watch the cooking channel?

204
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:34,710
- Hi, Chandler.     - Hey.

205
00:12:34,870 --> 00:12:37,710
Listen, I need that broiling pan that Joey borrowed the other day.

206
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:39,210
That was yours?

207
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:43,880
We used it when the duck was throwing up caterpillars.

208
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:47,430
Williams-Sonoma, fall catalog, page 27.

209
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,220
Expect it in 4 to 6 weeks.

210
00:12:50,930 --> 00:12:55,390
Hey. Joey's gonna be at the telethon for the rest of the day.

211
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:57,600
We have the whole place to ourselves.

212
00:12:57,770 --> 00:12:59,270
Yeah, so?

213
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:04,570
Just thought maybe you'd want to book some time with "the best you've ever had."

214
00:13:05,610 --> 00:13:07,490
You know what, champ?

215
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:09,030
I think I'll pass.

216
00:13:09,530 --> 00:13:12,040
- Why?     - Why?

217
00:13:25,050 --> 00:13:26,670
What's your point?

218
00:13:30,470 --> 00:13:32,890
PBS Telethon.

219
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:34,680
Hey, Joey.

220
00:13:34,850 --> 00:13:37,980
I just wanted to let you know that I found a selfless good deed.

221
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:41,400
I went down to the park and I let a bee sting me.

222
00:13:42,070 --> 00:13:44,440
What good is that going to do anybody?

223
00:13:44,610 --> 00:13:48,450
It helps the bee look tough in front of his bee friends.

224
00:13:48,910 --> 00:13:51,700
The bee is happy, and I am definitely not.

225
00:13:51,870 --> 00:13:55,540
You know, the bee probably died after he stung you.

226
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:02,340
Damn it!

227
00:14:03,710 --> 00:14:06,050
Back on in 30 seconds, people!

228
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:16,180
Excuse me, would you mind switching with me?

229
00:14:16,350 --> 00:14:18,640
No way. I'm in the shot, man.

230
00:14:19,350 --> 00:14:22,440
- You've been here all day!     - I'm taking pledges.

231
00:14:22,610 --> 00:14:25,400
And we're on three, two...

232
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:27,940
Welcome back to our fall telethon.

233
00:14:28,110 --> 00:14:30,910
If you've been enjoying the performance of Cirque du Soleil...

234
00:14:31,070 --> 00:14:35,120
...and you'd like to see more of the same kind of programming, it's very simple.

235
00:14:35,290 --> 00:14:38,410
All you have to do is call in and pledge...

236
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:44,210
...and at that time tell one of our volunteers what type of programming you...

237
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:47,550
Okay.

238
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:51,840
That's it. I cannot make this decision. It is too difficult.

239
00:14:52,010 --> 00:14:55,220
So I'm just going leave it entirely up to the gods of fate.

240
00:14:57,730 --> 00:14:59,350
A Magic 8 Ball?

241
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:02,230
You can't make this decision with a toy!

242
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:04,440
It's not a toy.

243
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:08,400
I don't know what else to do!

244
00:15:08,570 --> 00:15:12,860
I either keep my wife and lose one of my best friends...

245
00:15:13,030 --> 00:15:16,870
...or I keep my friend and get divorced for the second time before I'm 30.

246
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:20,370
So if anyone else has a better suggestion, let's hear it.

247
00:15:20,540 --> 00:15:23,000
Because I got nothing! Don't be shy.

248
00:15:23,170 --> 00:15:25,590
Any suggestion will do.

249
00:15:31,050 --> 00:15:32,880
Okay, then.

250
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:37,680
Here we go.

251
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:40,350
Magic 8 Ball...

252
00:15:40,520 --> 00:15:43,390
...should I never see Rachel again?

253
00:15:47,190 --> 00:15:48,360
"Ask Again Later."

254
00:15:50,150 --> 00:15:53,660
Later is not good enough!

255
00:15:59,450 --> 00:16:00,500
"Ask Again Later."

256
00:16:00,660 --> 00:16:01,700
What the hell?

257
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:05,170
This is broken! It is broken!

258
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:07,540
Let me see.

259
00:16:08,170 --> 00:16:10,960
Will Chandler have sex tonight?

260
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:12,920
"Don't Count On lt."

261
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:19,640
Seems like it works to me.

262
00:16:22,140 --> 00:16:23,940
PBS Telethon.

263
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:25,140
Hi, Joey.

264
00:16:25,310 --> 00:16:26,440
Hey, Pheebs.

265
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:28,150
I'd like to make a pledge.

266
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:30,400
I would like to donate $200.

267
00:16:30,570 --> 00:16:31,860
Two hundred dollars?

268
00:16:32,030 --> 00:16:34,860
You sure? After what Sesame Street did to you?

269
00:16:35,030 --> 00:16:38,570
I'm still mad at them, but I also know that they bring happiness...

270
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:41,240
...to lots of kids whose moms didn't kill themselves.

271
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:42,830
You know, so...

272
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:47,880
...by supporting them, I'm doing a good thing, but I'm not happy about it.

273
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:50,840
So there! A selfless good deed.

274
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,760
And you don't feel a little good about donating the money?

275
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:57,510
No, it sucks. I was saving up to buy a hamster.

276
00:16:58,050 --> 00:17:00,720
A hamster? Those things are, like, 10 bucks.

277
00:17:00,890 --> 00:17:03,390
Not the one I had my eye on.

278
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:07,650
It looks like we have surpassed last year's pledge total.

279
00:17:07,810 --> 00:17:08,900
Thank you!

280
00:17:09,690 --> 00:17:14,280
And the pledge that did it was taken by one of our volunteers.

281
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:20,660
Oh, boy! And may I say, one of our sharpest dressed volunteers.

282
00:17:20,830 --> 00:17:22,990
Mr. Joseph Tribbiani!

283
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,410
Oh, look!

284
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:26,250
Joey's on TV!

285
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:27,750
Isn't that great?

286
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:31,500
My pledge got Joey on TV! That makes me feel so...

287
00:17:31,670 --> 00:17:33,420
Oh, no!

288
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:41,220
Look...

289
00:17:41,390 --> 00:17:45,730
...maybe I got carried away before, but there's something you gotta know.

290
00:17:45,890 --> 00:17:50,440
If I'm the best, it's only because you made me the best.

291
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:54,360
Keep talking.

292
00:17:54,530 --> 00:17:56,610
I was nothing before you.

293
00:17:56,780 --> 00:17:59,280
Call the other girls and ask.

294
00:17:59,950 --> 00:18:02,200
Which wouldn't take long.

295
00:18:02,830 --> 00:18:06,160
But when I'm with you, and we're together...

296
00:18:06,330 --> 00:18:09,830
...oh, my God!

297
00:18:14,210 --> 00:18:17,630
- Really?     - Oh, my God!

298
00:18:20,090 --> 00:18:24,180
Now, I understand if you never want to sleep with me again.

299
00:18:24,350 --> 00:18:26,430
But that would be wrong.

300
00:18:27,270 --> 00:18:28,980
We're too good.

301
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:32,690
We owe it to sex!

302
00:18:34,230 --> 00:18:36,320
Well, if we owe it!

303
00:18:38,650 --> 00:18:39,990
Oh, my!

304
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:43,030
When is Joey gonna be home?

305
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:46,370
I was kind of hoping we could do this without him.

306
00:18:47,870 --> 00:18:51,080
No, no, no! Leave the gloves on.

307
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:52,960
But I just cleaned the bathroom.

308
00:18:53,130 --> 00:18:55,670
- Yeah, why don't we lose the gloves?     - Yeah.

309
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:00,930
All right. Let's show them how it's done.

310
00:19:01,090 --> 00:19:02,970
Okay. Ow!

311
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:07,600
- That wasn't part of it.      - I know.

312
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:24,740
Hi. You ready? We're going to be late.

313
00:19:24,910 --> 00:19:28,080
- For what?     - For Stella, remember?

314
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:31,160
She's getting her groove back in 20 minutes.

315
00:19:32,540 --> 00:19:35,750
Yeah, I totally forgot about that.

316
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:39,840
Mind if I take a rain check? I'm waiting for a call from Emily.

317
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:42,680
Sure, I guess.

318
00:19:42,840 --> 00:19:46,550
Hey, I hear you don't have to go to London. Yay.

319
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:52,520
It's not that easy. There's still a lot of relationship stuff.

320
00:19:52,690 --> 00:19:54,100
Like what?

321
00:19:54,270 --> 00:19:55,770
Just stuff.

322
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:59,940
You know, kind of what Emily wants.

323
00:20:00,490 --> 00:20:02,530
Why don't you talk to me about it? Maybe I can help.

324
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:07,330
No, no, you can't help.

325
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:12,500
I mean, I kind of have to do this without your help.

326
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:14,790
Well, I...

327
00:20:15,330 --> 00:20:19,880
I know you can do that too. I'm just saying if you need somebody to talk to...

328
00:20:20,550 --> 00:20:22,260
Hi.

329
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:25,180
Thanks.

330
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:32,180
Ross, look, whatever this relationship stuff is that Emily wants...

331
00:20:32,350 --> 00:20:34,310
...just give it to her.

332
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:37,020
The bottom line is that you love her.

333
00:20:37,190 --> 00:20:39,400
So just fix whatever she wants fixed.

334
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:41,530
Just do it.

335
00:20:43,150 --> 00:20:47,490
You're going to have to try. You'll just hate yourself if you don't.

336
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:53,290
Come on, answer it! It's driving me crazy.

337
00:20:54,830 --> 00:20:56,040
Hello?

338
00:20:56,540 --> 00:20:58,330
Hi, sweetie.

339
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:00,460
Good.

340
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:04,840
Look. Yes, I've been thinking...

341
00:21:05,010 --> 00:21:08,930
...about that thing you wanted me to do...

342
00:21:09,100 --> 00:21:12,930
...and I can do it.

343
00:21:15,390 --> 00:21:18,020
So will you come to New York?

344
00:21:19,520 --> 00:21:20,650
What?

345
00:22:00,230 --> 00:22:02,520
- Never done that before.     - Nope.

